#
# Counter-example for the math: slice's thin math:FlagshipScenarioShape: a
# gmeow:FlagshipScenario that binds ALL links — gmeow:demonstratedByExample,
# gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency, gmeow:demonstratedByProducer,
# gmeow:guardedByCounterExample, AND gmeow:enforcesFailureClass — so the shared
# cardinalities are satisfied, but gmeow:enforcesFailureClass names math:Set, a real
# class that is NOT a math:MathConformanceFailure subclass. The slice's failure-range
# sh:sparql fires, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent: an acceptance
# scenario whose enforcing failure class is not a typed conformance failure is unwired by
# value (math:UnwiredFlagshipScenario).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecFlagshipNonFailureClass).
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:nonFailureClassScenario a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByExample "examples/e8-symmetry.ttl" ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/cqE8RootSystem> ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByProducer "math::producers::e8_weyl_order" ;
    gmeow:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl" ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass math:Set .
